cves.mitigation:
Disable DNS recursion on the BIG-IP system

To disable DNS recursion on the BIG-IP system, perform the following steps:

Log in to the Configuration utility.
Navigate to DNS > Zones > ZoneRunner > named Configuration.
In the Options box, scroll down to the options section, find the recursion yes; statement, and edit it to read recursion no;.
Select Update.

Alternatively, you can mitigate this vulnerability by disabling the following algorithms in your BIND configuration using the disable-algorithms option:

ECDSAP256SHA256
ECDSAP384SHA384

Impact of action: After you disable these algorithms, the BIG-IP system treats zones signed with these algorithms as insecure.

The disable-algorithms statement should be used in a global options clause in your BIND configuration. For example, the following disable-algorithms statement disables the ECDSAP256SHA256 and ECDSAP384SHA384 algorithms for all domains:

disable-algorithms "." {
        "ECDSAP256SHA256";
        "ECDSAP384SHA384";
    };

To mitigate this vulnerability, you can use a unique and isolated web browser when managing the BIG-IP or BIG-IQ system.

This attack cannot be prevented if you have authenticated to iControl SOAP in the web browser with basic authentication. This authentication mechanism is uncommon and is different from using the login page for the Configuration utility. F5 recommends that you do not authenticate with basic authentication in the web browser. If an authentication window for basic authentication pops up on the web browser, do not provide credentials.

