Create a new iRule based on the _sys_auth_ssl_ocsp iRule in the BIG-IP iRule list, which includes the additional check iRule block. To do so, complete the following procedure:

Go to Local Traffic > iRules > iRule List.
Select Create.
Give the iRule a name, for example:

sys_auth_ssl_ocsp_additional_check.

Copy the following iRule and paste it in the Definition box:

Note: If you are using a custom SSL OCSP Authentication iRule, ensure you modify the custom iRule and add the "additional check" block as shown in the sample iRule.

when CLIENT_ACCEPTED {
        set tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_sid 0
        set tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_done 0
    }
    when CLIENTSSL_CLIENTCERT {
        if {[SSL::cert count] == 0} {
            return
        }
    #====== additional check=========
        if {[SSL::verify_result] != 0} {
             return
        }
    #================================
        set tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_done 0
        if {$tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_sid == 0} {
            set tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_sid [AUTH::start pam default_ssl_ocsp]
            if {[info exists tmm_auth_subscription]} {
                AUTH::subscribe $tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_sid
            }
        }
        AUTH::cert_credential $tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_sid [SSL::cert 0]
        AUTH::cert_issuer_credential $tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_sid [SSL::cert issuer 0]
        AUTH::authenticate $tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_sid
        SSL::handshake hold
    }
    when CLIENTSSL_HANDSHAKE {
        set tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_done 1
    }
    when AUTH_RESULT {
        if {[info exists tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_sid] and \
            ($tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_sid == [AUTH::last_event_session_id])} {
            set tmm_auth_status [AUTH::status]
            if {$tmm_auth_status == 0} {
                set tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_done 1
                SSL::handshake resume
            } elseif {$tmm_auth_status != -1 || $tmm_auth_ssl_ocsp_done == 0} {
                reject
            }
        }
    }
Select Finished.
Go to Local Traffic > Profiles > Authentication > Profiles.
